=====================================================================
KNOWN GAPS
=====================================================================

Three vectorizer gaps remain, all needing genuinely new capability
rather than the loosening of an over-tight gate:

  argmax / argmin   two mutually-dependent live-out reductions;
                    rejected by vect_is_simple_use.
  prefix sum        needs a scan pattern.
  histogram         needs conflict detection for scatter-add.

Audited and deliberately not changed: software prefetching is measured
harmful on this core (-fprefetch-loop-arrays costs about 6% on 32 MB
streams, and X86_TUNE_SOFTWARE_PREFETCHING_BENEFICIAL correctly excludes
all Intel parts); FMA accumulator depth is already sufficient (GCC emits
four accumulators and the auto-vectorized dot product is
bandwidth-bound); ACO's register-window scan in get_reg_simple has a
data-dependent early break and is unvectorizable in principle.

