+@opindex ftree-loop-invdiv
+@opindex fno-tree-loop-invdiv
+@item -ftree-loop-invdiv
+Replace an integer division or modulo whose divisor is invariant in a
+loop, but is not a compile-time constant, with a reciprocal
+(``magic number'') multiply.  Both signed and unsigned divisions are
+handled; the signed case divides the absolute values and fixes up the
+sign.  The magic number is derived once in the
+loop preheader with a single division, and the loop body is left with a
+widening highpart multiply and a few cheap integer operations.  Unlike
+loop versioning for a power-of-two divisor this needs no runtime test and
+no code duplication, because the sequence used is correct for every
+divisor value, and it lets the resulting loop be vectorized.  Enabled by
+default at @option{-O2} and above, except when optimizing for size.
+
 @opindex ftree-loop-ivcanon
 @opindex fno-tree-loop-ivcanon
 @item -ftree-loop-ivcanon
